    "towerM": 17,
    "text": {
      "en": "Stands on the summit Skužučohkka south of Berlevåg on the Barents Sea coast and watches East Finnmark and the sea beyond. It is MET Norway's easternmost radar, opened in 2012, and its antenna was mounted unusually high so that a nearby building would not block its view."
    },
