    "system": "Selex METEOR 635CDP10",
    "band": "C",
    "dualPol": true,
    "since": "2010",
    "towerM": 13.5,
    "text": {
      "en": "Stands on Nielsåsen on the Hurum peninsula, now part of Asker, 363 m above sea level. It is the radar closest to Oslo and watches central Eastern Norway and the Oslofjord. It went into service in 2010, replacing an older radar at Hagahogget in Asker."
    },
