    "text": {
      "en": "Stands on Nagelen in the Olsøyheia hills of Indre Fosen, across the fjord from Trondheim, 616 m above sea level, and watches Trøndelag, part of Møre og Romsdal and the fishing banks offshore. The site opened in 2002; in 2018 its radar, then MET Norway's oldest, was replaced by a dual-polarisation unit."
